<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  RUT_FungusEating.xml       UtinniPatches — CAVERNS_PARITY_BUILD_1 ruling 4

  A donor-free twin of the neutral position on vanilla Ideology's FungusEating
  issue. The Salvation (src/Jawa/ideoligion/The Salvation.rid) held
  BMT_FungusEating_DontCare, owned by Biomes! Caverns
  (biomesteam.biomescaverns) — a donor scheduled for the cut. A .rid holding a
  defName no installed mod defines fails to load: Scribe reports
  "Could not load reference to ..." and no mod change repairs it, because the
  dead name is inside the file. So the clan's own doctrine cannot depend on a
  donor def.

  The ISSUE needs no twin: FungusEating is vanilla Ideology
  (ludeon.rimworld.ideology), measured from the live def dump
  2026-09-18T17-31-09Z. Only the "don't care" POSITION was donor-owned —
  Ideology itself ships only Preferred and Despised.

  Field-for-field equal to the donor as the dump reports it: issue
  FungusEating, impact Low, displayOrderInIssue 5, no comps (a neutral
  position is defined by the absence of thought comps, not by any of its
  own), selectionWeight 1 and defaultSelectionWeight 0 left at their
  defaults. The label and description are ours.

  MayRequire guards the DLC the issue comes from; with Ideology off the def is
  skipped rather than loading against a missing issue.
-->
<Defs>

  <PreceptDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
    <defName>RUT_FungusEating_DontCare</defName>
    <issue>FungusEating</issue>
    <label>don't care</label>
    <description>Fungus is food like any other. It feeds no reverence and earns no disgust.</description>
    <impact>Low</impact>
    <displayOrderInIssue>5</displayOrderInIssue>
  </PreceptDef>

</Defs>
